WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Many teams use a load balancer because clients want one endpoint.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.290
Chat UIs, coding assistants, automation scripts,

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.000
and internal tools are easier to configure when they all call a single base URL.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.230
A reverse proxy, gateway,

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:15.822
or load balancer can present that endpoint while distributing work across multiple local

00:00:15.822 --> 00:00:16.750
LLM servers.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.200
Compatibility depends on details.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.000
Endpoint paths must match client expectations.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.995
Model names may need stable aliases.

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:26.495
Headers may carry authentication, tracing, or streaming preferences.

00:00:26.495 --> 00:00:29.500
Response fields and error codes should remain understandable to the client.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.560
A setup that works for one script may still fail for a coding assistant if it changes

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.240
streaming or error behavior.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:37.500
Streaming compatibility is a common failure point.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.500
Some proxies buffer responses by default,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.000
turning an interactive token stream into a long pause followed by a complete answer.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Others apply idle timeouts that interrupt slow generations.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
If a client expects server-sent events or chunked output,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.250
the entire path from client to backend must preserve that behavior.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.500
Authentication and testing belong in the design.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.210
A local endpoint may process source code, private documents, prompts, outputs,

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.665
and accidental secrets.

00:01:00.665 --> 00:01:03.000
Centralizing access can simplify controls,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.445
but it also makes the gateway sensitive infrastructure.

00:01:05.445 --> 00:01:09.973
Before replacing direct backend connections, test the real chat UI, coding assistant,

00:01:09.973 --> 00:01:13.820
scripts, model selection, streaming, cancellation, retries, long prompts,

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.000
and error handling.
